if you want to have success on YouTube  making videos and have people really  relate to them and showcase yourself as  an expert then you have to believe  passionately in what you're talking  about and share things that are  important to you hi I'm Evan Carmichael  and I believe that hungry entrepreneurs  deserve help so today i'm answering a  question from one of my readers nick who  wrote in to say he was asked about my  videos hi of them I'm in the process of  improving my video communications and I  think yours are really good what's the  secret other than your incredible talent  Thank You Nick and wrote in with  specific questions that I'm going to get  into so first one is how did you get so  good was a natural talent lots of  practice did you get coach did you do  training I don't think I'm particularly  good at it I've done some speaking  before so that may have helped a little  bit but i don't think i have natural  talent for it it did take a lot of  practice if you go back and look at my  earlier videos they were really bad some  of them i'm so embarrassed about that i  want to take down but people keep  watching them and leaving comments on  them that are positive so i keep them up  but i really want to take them down  anyway so it has taken a lot of practice  i have a couple hundred videos now up on  youtube and i think the biggest thing  with practice is just getting used to  talking to the camera I found when I was  getting started I was a little nervous  when i pressed record I was fine before  it sounded great but then you stand in  front of the camera you look right into  it and you press record and I don't know  I got shaky my heart was beating so it  sweating a little bit so as you do more  of those it gets easier I also found  that when people were around me watching  or even just working on their own thing  I got more nervous and I didn't create a  good quality video so as you do more you  do get more comfortable front of the  camera so I think that's helped I also  did trying to model success something  obviously I believe in modeling success  just like you're doing where you're  watching my videos and saying hey I like  what everyone's doing I'm going to try  to model that I did the same thing when  I was starting and looked at other  channels that I liked and tried to model  what they were doing and still do now I  still try to see you know what pieces I  could pull from what other people are  doing and apply it to my own videos as  well and then third I work with an agent  in New York and they have given me some  feedback and tips on my videos and I try  to apply those  as well but the most important thing  from all of that is really you have to  strongly believe in the message of each  video it's so important and I think in  my earlier videos I was passionate about  them but I didn't raise the stakes  enough I didn't make it important enough  and what I try to think about now is  when somebody asked me a question that  my answer can help make the difference  between them giving up or keep on going  I have to convince them to follow the  advice I have to make it important for  them and so you should try to apply that  to your videos as well you have great  advice but if you deliver it in a blend  or boring way or it sounds like you're  reading something it's not going to hit  them you know you could say the same  thing with a lot of excitement and  importance and urgency or really boring  and I'm trying to memorize my script and  it doesn't come out very cleanly and  that'll make all the difference so I try  to make an important I try to think of  that person and having an impact on them  and that one video I have that one  chance every time I do a video to be  able to have an impact on that one  person's life and if they don't change  part of that is on me that's my  responsibility because I didn't do  enough to really convince them through  the video that this is the correct path  that they should take so that's helped a  lot second question when you talk to the  camera do you have a script behind the  camera I never use a script I find that  if you're trying to memorize something  or if you're trying to read something  people can tell great you see people  looking off to the side like this or  trying to read in and and see what the  words are so they say it exactly right  the problem is is always boring you  never say things with the right amount  of passion if you're reading it off a  script and it's way more important to  get your point across it's way more  important to have the feeling and energy  and passion to convince somebody that  what you're saying is really the path  they should take  that comes not from reading a script  it's not so much what you say it's how  you say it so don't worry about getting  every single word right because it's  going to stress you out neither dad the  beginning to you know I didn't read from  a script but i memorize things and I  tried to get everything out exactly and  we do lots of cuts and takes and it  never looked good so now when a message  comes in i'll look at it on my phone  really quickly i might come up with a  couple points in my head and then i'll  just get in front of the camera and talk  and again try to think about talking to  that person and having an impact with  each video that I make and if I make  mistakes along the way I've already made  a few in this video I just keep rolling  you keep going with it because that's  part of the process of making videos and  I think it makes people think you're  more human and are more willing to  listen to the things that you're saying  what equipment do you use number three  questions so I don't believe in spending  money till I'm making money and so I  didn't want to go out and spend tons of  money on the all the equipment because I  didn't know if it would make money but  also I didn't know if I would stick with  it you know a lot of entrepreneurs get  excited about new projects go buy all  the equipment by tons of inventory for  their new idea and then a couple months  later I get bored of it and move on to  something else and meanwhile you spent  all this money on this equipment that  you're not using so I started off really  simple really dead easy it was with my  own flip camera and if you watch some of  the earlier videos might see if shaking  a little bit very embarrassing but again  people like them the production quality  is really poor the lighting sucks the  audio is really bad and then slowly as i  learned the techniques behind video  production as well as making a little  bit of money I poured it back into the  videos so now i use a sony handycam i  bought it from costco i bought all my  stuff from costco because they have a 90  day return policy compared to other  stores that were seven or 14 so it gives  you the chance to really test out the  products make sure you like it before  you really commit to it sony handycam  the reason why I got it is because it  has an external mic jack so people were  complaining earlier about my videos that  they couldn't hear me properly the audio  quality wasn't great  so needed a camera with an external  microphone and then i went to the sony  store and bought this microphone eighty  or ninety dollars that you just clip in  and it works in there and then the other  thing i use is a tripod just picked it  up from my local camera store and that's  all i use i don't really use much  lighting now i'm doing this video in my  office there's a window in front of me  so I get the light hitting my face and  that's it i use my phone to kind of give  me the clues as to what to talk about  next and that's equipment that I use so  it's still pretty low budget but enough  to get everything going i didn't want  super high production quality as well  because I don't know sometimes that that  makes it look not very authentic so  that's what i'm using right now and last  do you edit the videos so again i don't  like spending money till i'm making  money so at the beginning I learned  everything myself I started with windows  movie maker that comes default with  every you know windows computer that you  buy and then I moved up the Camtasia and  learn how to do the video editing and it  was really poor you know I wasn't great  at it but it was enough to put it up and  get it up on the website and then again  as I started making money I quickly  looked at okay how can i delegate this  because of a look at what I'm doing with  the videos the best use of my time is  getting in front of the camera and doing  more videos and answering questions and  helping people it's not trying to figure  out how to be a video editor because I'm  not really good at it and it's really  not the best use of my time on going so  as soon as I started making money I  quickly found somebody who could edit  and produce and do all the fancy stuff  with my videos again it's not crazy and  we have the intro you know extra a  couple touch-ups you know we're moving  me at the beginning testing the  microphone and all that kind of stuff  you know picking my nose whatever it is  but yeah I started off doing everything  myself and then slowly expanded and  brought on people to help me with it so  that's it hopefully Nick that helped out  good luck with your videos if you want  to send me your first couple that you do  I'd love to be able to take a look at it  and give you some some advice for those  are you watching if you liked the video  please give it a thumbs up below I  always love seeing those come in  and if you have a comment about this  video or a question for your business I  want to try to help answer it for you  please leave it in the comments section  below it's really one of the best parts  of my day is watching those YouTube  comments come in so thank you and I'll  see you on the next episode  you

